{
 "name": "Osiris Piano (music-production build)",
 "comment": "Built from Osiris Piano by Karoryfer Samples, CC0 1.0. Source: https://github.com/sfzinstruments/Osiris_Piano at 18c6afccb60cff458edbf7c394571783e074e1e9. A grand piano sampled on all 52 white keys A0-C8 in two velocity layers, once with the dampers down (UC) and once with the sustain pedal held (UC-Sus), each take recorded by three microphone pairs. As in the library's own program, the three pairs are summed at full level, here sample-aligned into one stereo take. A SoundFont cannot change recordings with the pedal, so there are two presets: pedal up (program 0) and pedal down (bank 1, program 0). The library names notes an octave below standard pitch (its A3 sounds A4). Kept from the library: its tuning (the treble is stretched sharp, as pianos are tuned, so no intonation correction is applied) and its damper release by register, 1.0 s in the bass to 0.42 s in the treble, with no dampers from F#6. Changes: the key noise before each hammer strike (about 25 ms) is trimmed to the last few milliseconds so the piano plays on the beat; the two velocity layers are levelled to the same early RMS so the velocity curve, not a step at 64, sets loudness; a take louder or softer than its neighbours is pulled toward them (at most 6 dB); the pedal-up soft B4 that the library lacks is covered by its neighbours; the bank sits 6 dB lower than the others so no take is limited at full scale; notes cut at 12 s (pedal up) or 15 s (pedal down) with a 50 ms fade; 16-bit TPDF dither.",
 "copyright": "Source samples CC0 1.0 (Karoryfer Samples, Osiris Piano)",
 "target_rms": 0.04,
